find . -print 

where . represent's the current directory

-print present's . and .. --> for the parent

-maxdepth (Top) 

-mindepth (Bottom)


find . -maxdepth 2 "f*" -print

./f1..
./f1../f1.1...

Using Find Command Based On The File Type:
=========================================

find . -type d -print

f - file
d - directory
l - symbolic link
s - socket
b - block device


-atime (access time)
-mtime (modification time)
-ctime (change time)

find . -type f -atime -7 print

find . -type f -mtime +7 print

find . -type f -ctime -7 print

The following command is used to print the file's that are newer the file.txt

find . -type f -newer file.txt -print

The following command is used to delete the file's that match

find . -type f -new "f*" -delete

